# Agent Definition Template

> This template defines the structure that the Pipeline Generator uses to produce
> customer-specific agent definition files. Variables in `{{VARIABLE}}` are replaced
> during generation.
>
> **CRITICAL:** Every variable MUST be resolved with SPECIFIC content from the contract.
> NEVER use generic placeholder text. If a variable cannot be resolved, the generator
> must read the contract again and extract the specific content.
>
> **ANTI-PATTERNS (NEVER produce these):**
> - `{{WORKFLOW_INSTRUCTIONS}}` → "Execute contract workflow logic" ❌ (must be full step-by-step from contract)
> - `{{INPUTS}}` → "Contract-required upstream artifacts" ❌ (must list exact artifacts from contract)
> - `{{OUTPUTS}}` → "Stage outputs" ❌ (must list exact artifacts from contract)
> - `{{QUALITY_CHECKLIST_FROM_CONTRACT}}` → "Address this contract outcome" ❌ (must include full descriptive text)
> - `{{COMPLETION_CRITERIA}}` → Same 4 lines for every agent ❌ (must be agent-specific)

