## Variable Resolution

| Variable | Source | Expected Content (NOT generic) |
|----------|--------|-------------------------------|
| `AGENT_DISPLAY_NAME` | Contract → agent_name | e.g., "Ticket Analyzer" |
| `AGENT_DESCRIPTION` | Contract → Role (first sentence) | e.g., "Fetches ticket context and classifies for routing" |
| `RESOLVED_MODEL` | Contract model_tier → Customer's model mapping | e.g., "gpt-4o" |
| `ARGUMENT_HINT` | Contract → argument_hint or generated from inputs | e.g., "Ticket ID or requirement file path" |
| `CONTRACT_ID` | Contract → contract_id | e.g., "AC-000" |
| `PIPELINE_POSITION` | Contract → pipeline_position | e.g., "0" |
| `MODEL_TIER` | Contract → model_tier | e.g., "reasoning" |
| `TOOLS` | Contract tool_categories → resolved to platform tools | e.g., ["execute", "read", "edit"] |
| `HOOKS` | Hook IDs applicable to this agent (from hooks.json) | e.g., ["guard_destructive", "otel_telemetry"] |
| `ROLE_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Role section (verbatim) | Full role paragraph from contract |
| `PRIME_DIRECTIVE_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Prime Directive (verbatim) | Exact quote from contract |
| `CUSTOMER_GUARDRAILS` | Onboarding answers → Agent Behavioral Guardrails | Customer's specific guardrails list |
| `AGENT_SLUG` | Agent name in kebab-case (e.g., `agent0_ticket_analyzer`) | Used for file references |
| `INPUTS` | Contract → Inputs table (EXACT rows, not generic) | Every artifact row from contract's Inputs table |
| `INPUT_VALIDATION_RULES` | Contract → Input Validation section (specific rules per input) | e.g., "Ticket ID must match prefix regex" |
| `OUTPUTS` | Contract → Outputs table (EXACT rows, not generic) | Every artifact row from contract's Outputs table |
| `OUTPUT_HANDLING_RULES` | Contract → specific write paths, validation, handoff per output | e.g., "Write ticket_analysis.md to outputs/<ID>/" |
| `WORKFLOW_INSTRUCTIONS` | Contract → Workflow Logic (ALL steps with conditions/actions/outputs) | Full numbered step-by-step, typically 30-100 lines |
| `USE_MCP` | True if platform uses MCP integration | Boolean |
| `MCP_TOOL_REFERENCES` | MCP server/tool invocation instructions from `.mcp.json` | Server names and usage |
| `USE_CONNECTOR_SKILLS` | True if platform uses API-based Connector Skills | Boolean |
| `SKILL_REFERENCES` | Generated skills matching contract skill references | Skill paths and purposes |
| `CHECKPOINTING_STRATEGY` | Generated: agent-specific state fields, save triggers, file path, format example | e.g., "Save ticket_id, classification, repo_candidates after step 6" |
| `RESUME_PROTOCOL` | Generated: agent-specific resume from checkpoint with step references | e.g., "If classification exists, skip steps 1-5, resume from step 6" |
| `RERUN_PROTOCOL` | Generated: agent-specific cascade effects and affected steps | e.g., "If reclassify requested, invalidate downstream routing" |
| `ACCESS_RESTRICTIONS_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Access Restrictions table | Permission table from contract |
| `HOOK_TABLE` | Generated table rows: id, event, blocking, purpose per hook | Full hook config rows |
| `QUALITY_CHECKLIST_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Key Outcomes with FULL descriptive text | e.g., "[OUTCOME-FETCH] All relevant ticket context retrieved and materialized" |
| `COMPLETION_CRITERIA` | Generated: explicit conditions for agent to be considered done |
| `AGENT_VERSION` | Contract → version |
